<Layout title="Privacy — Seven Sins" description="How Seven Sins handles local quiz answers, downloaded result images, shared links, and hosting requests."><article class="article-page"><a class="back-home" href="/">← Back to the test</a><h1>Your answers.<br/>Your device.</h1><p class="lead">The questionnaire calculates your scores and generates your result image in your browser. We do not send your individual quiz answers to a server.</p><h2>Saved progress</h2><p>We use your browser’s local storage to remember answers and the current question. This lets you refresh or return on the same browser and continue. Start over clears the saved quiz by replacing it with empty answers. You can also clear this site’s data in your browser settings. If local storage is unavailable, the quiz works for the current page session, but progress may be lost when you close or refresh it.</p><h2>Result images and links</h2><p>Downloading a PNG creates the image locally. A shared result link includes the test version and seven scores in the URL fragment (the part after #). Anyone who receives the link can view those scores. The link contains no individual answers or name. URL fragments are not normally included in HTTP requests, but messaging services, browser sync, or anyone receiving the full link may have access to them.</p><h2>Hosting and analytics</h2><p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Loading a page sends ordinary connection information, such as your IP address, requested path, browser information, and request time, to the hosting provider. Cloudflare may process this information to deliver and protect the site under its own policies.</p><p>We use Google Analytics 4 to understand visits and use of the site. Google may use cookies and process information such as device and browser details, approximate location, and page activity. We configure the page address without the query string or fragment; Google Analytics may also collect page URLs and query parameters depending on its settings, so avoid putting sensitive information in a URL. Learn more about <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Links to IPIP and the project repository take you to other services with their own privacy practices. We self-host the website fonts, so viewing this site does not require a Google Fonts request.</p><h2>Questions or problems</h2><p>You can <a href="https://github.com/toolution/seven-deadly-sins-test/issues">report a site issue</a>. Do not include private answers or personal information in a public issue. This notice was updated on November 23, 2026.</p></article></Layout>
